+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_orig_mnqwy3c7heztgmrygvtdmnjshbrdimlggu4damjqgvsgkna","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 1: Basic FIFO Queue\n2\t\n3\tImplement a `TaskQueue` class with the following interface:\n4\t\n5\t## Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`enqueue(payload)`** - Add a task to the queue. Returns the created task object.\n8\t- **`dequeue()`** - Remove and return the next task in FIFO order. Returns `null` if the queue is empty. Sets the task status to `processing`.\n9\t- **`size()`** - Return the number of pending tasks in the queue.\n10\t\n11\t## Task Object\n12\t\n13\tEach task has the following properties:\n14\t\n15\t| Property    | Type     | Description                                    |\n16\t|-------------|----------|------------------------------------------------|\n17\t| `id`        | `string` | Auto-generated unique identifier (UUID format) |\n18\t| `payload`   | `any`    | The data associated with the task              |\n19\t| `status`    | `string` | One of: `pending`, `processing`, `completed`, `failed` |\n20\t| `createdAt` | `Date`   | Timestamp when the task was created            |\n21\t\n22\t## Requirements\n23\t\n24\t- Tasks are returned in the order they were added (First-In, First-Out)\n25\t- Each task gets a unique `id` automatically assigned\n26\t- New tasks start with `status: 'pending'`\n27\t- When dequeued, task status changes to `'processing'`\n28\t- `dequeue()` returns `null` when the queue is empty\n29\t\n30\t## Export\n31\t\n32\tExport the `TaskQueue` class as a named export from `src/index.ts`.\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"571ce18c-c8b7-419f-ba15-a05fb762ca58","uuid":"e0e74477-71bd-47f3-8e18-4986c2f50f58","timestamp":"2026-06-17T21:33:40.144Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/phases/phase-01.md","content":"# Phase 1: Basic FIFO Queue\n\nImplement a `TaskQueue` class with the following interface:\n\n## Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(payload)`** - Add a task to the queue. Returns the created task object.\n- **`dequeue()`** - Remove and return the next task in FIFO order. Returns `null` if the queue is empty. Sets the task status to `processing`.\n- **`size()`** - Return the number of pending tasks in the queue.\n\n## Task Object\n\nEach task has the following properties:\n\n| Property    | Type     | Description                                    |\n|-------------|----------|------------------------------------------------|\n| `id`        | `string` | Auto-generated unique identifier (UUID format) |\n| `payload`   | `any`    | The data associated with the task              |\n| `status`    | `string` | One of: `pending`, `processing`, `completed`, `failed` |\n| `createdAt` | `Date`   | Timestamp when the task was created            |\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Tasks are returned in the order they were added (First-In, First-Out)\n- Each task gets a unique `id` automatically assigned\n- New tasks start with `status: 'pending'`\n- When dequeued, task status changes to `'processing'`\n- `dequeue()` returns `null` when the queue is empty\n\n## Export\n\nExport the `TaskQueue` class as a named export from `src/index.ts`.\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}}}
